## Why This Is Asked
Understanding cross-language adapter strategies with strict latency and memory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- PEFT vs full fine-tuning in multi-language QA
- Adapter injection points (attention vs MLP)
- Language tagging vs per-language adapters
- Latency/memory budgeting and rollback plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo adapter injection sketch
function attachAdapters(model, keys) {
  for (const m of model.modules()) {
    if (m instanceof AttentionLayer || m instanceof MLP) {
      m.addAdapter({rank: 8, name: keys.next()});
    }
  }
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift between languages post-deployment?
- What failure modes require bypassing adapters and using base model instead?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-world ability to build autonomous, tool-using planning with LangChain, handling failures and idempotence under latency.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain Tools orchestration
- Planning/Autogen style decomposition
- Idempotence and retry semantics
- Observability and testing strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal pseudoplanner
async function planIncident(incident, tools){
  const steps = [];
  if (incident.severity>3) steps.push({name:'fetchMetrics', tool:'metrics_api'});
  steps.push({name:'lookupRunbook', tool:'runbooks_db'});
  steps.push({name:'ensureTicket', tool:'ticket_api'});
  return steps;
}
```

